Pseudo-random number generators (crates/bb-core/src/rng.rs)

SplitMix64 and xoshiro256** are implemented from their published descriptions:
  - G. L. Steele Jr., D. Lea, C. H. Flood, "Fast splittable pseudorandom number generators",
    OOPSLA 2014.
  - D. Blackman, S. Vigna, "Scrambled linear pseudorandom number generators",
    ACM Transactions on Mathematical Software, 2021. https://prng.di.unimi.it/
    The reference implementations are dedicated to the public domain by their authors.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Strategy formulas (crates/bb-strategies)

The Avellaneda-Stoikov strategy is an original implementation of the formulas published in:
  - M. Avellaneda, S. Stoikov, "High-frequency trading in a limit order book",
    Quantitative Finance 8(3), 2008.
No third-party strategy code is included.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Market data

No market data from any vendor or exchange is included in this repository. Datasets used by the
tests and the bundled demonstration are generated by BlackBox HFT itself.
